<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marduk-nadin-ahhe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1099–1082 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marduk-nadin-ahhe was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> of the Second Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a>, reigning from about 1099 to 1082 BCE, and a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-i">Nebuchadnezzar I</a>. He raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and carried off statues of gods from Ekallatum, but the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-i">Tiglath-Pileser I</a> struck back, raiding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> and burning palaces in Babylon. His later years were marked by famine and Aramean incursions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marduk-nadin-ahhe.jpg" alt="Marduk-nadin-ahhe" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Babylon)Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Babylonian_-_Boundary_Stone_-_Walters_2110.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
